man: Look up scdoc as a native dependency

scdoc is a build tool, so it has to be found in the native sysroot when
cross compiling. Otherwise the man pages are silently skipped.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Erik Sallmann <e.sallmann@kunbus.com>

diff --git a/man/meson.build b/man/meson.build
index 9c067eb..aad05d5 100644
--- a/man/meson.build
+++ b/man/meson.build
@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@ man_page_sources = files(
   'pibridge-shutdown.8.scd'
 )
 
-scdoc = dependency('scdoc', required: get_option('man-pages'))
+scdoc = dependency('scdoc', native: true, required: get_option('man-pages'))
 if scdoc.found()
   scdoc_prog = find_program(scdoc.get_variable(pkgconfig: 'scdoc'), native: true)
   mandir = get_option('mandir')
